B wrapper done. **Step 3: top edits**. Changes to prj9's aurora_udp_bridge.v:

1. Header comment update (dual-cage)
2. Ports: add sfpb_rx_p/n, sfpb_tx_p/n, sfpb_tx_disable, sfpb_rs0, sfpb_rs1
3. A instance: aurora_64b66b_0_support → aurora_64b66b_0_support_ext + connect new ports (.refclk1_out(sh_refclk), .gt_qpllclk_quad1_out(sh_qpllclk), .gt_qpllrefclk_quad1_out(sh_qpllrefclk), .gt_qplllock_quad1_out(sh_qplllock), .gt_qpllrefclklost_quad1_out(sh_qpllrefclklost), .ext_qpllreset_in(b_qpllreset))
4. B section: wires + instance + echo fifo + assigns
5. aurora_rst: ~sys_rst_n | ~(channel_up & channel_up_b); led_link = channel_up & channel_up_b
6. debug taps

The echo FIFO: axis_data_fifo_64b instantiation. Ports (v2.0 sync mode): 
- s_axis_aclk
- s_axis_tvalid/tready/tdata/tlast? — I fold tkeep+tlast into tdata[79:0]? I decided: TDATA_NUM_BYTES=10 → tdata[79:0] = {8'b0? or spare, tlast, tkeep, tdata}: bit [71:64]=tkeep, bit 72=tlast? With 80 bits: [79:73] spare 7 bits, [72]=tlast, [71:64]=tkeep, [63:0]=data.
- Wait — does axis_data_fifo v2.0 have native TLAST port even if unused? The IP core ports: s_axis_tdata, s_axis_tkeep, s_axis_tlast, s_axis_tuser, s_axis_tstrb... depends on HAS_* params — defaults: HAS_TLAST? In v2.0 I believe default includes TLAST only if... ugh. To be safe my instantiation will connect ONLY s_axis_aclk/tvalid/tready/tdata and m_* — if the core has extra input ports (tlast etc.) unconnected → warnings, not errors (unconnected input ports default X/z in sim but synth treats as tie-off... unconnected INPUT ports in synthesis = warning, treated as 0? For IP cores with required inputs it can be an elaboration error "formal port not connected"... IP instantiation from XCI stub: unconnected optional ports are OK (they get pruned by param). Since I'm creating the IP myself in create_project.tcl, I'll configure HAS_TLAST=false/HAS_TKEEP=false/TUSER_WIDTH=0 explicitly — then stub has ONLY tdata/tvalid/tready. Clean.

Actually — axis_data_fifo 2.0 params (from memory of PG053):
- CONFIG.TDATA_NUM_BYTES (int)
- CONFIG.TDEST_WIDTH, CONFIG.TID_WIDTH, CONFIG.TUSER_WIDTH  
- CONFIG.HAS_TLAST (bool) — hmm, not sure this exists; TLAST might be inherent to AXIS... In axis_data_fifo, TLAST exists when FIFO_MODE=2 (packet). For FIFO_MODE=1? I recall the GUI showing "Enable TLAST" tied to packet mode. To be safe: set FIFO_MODE=2 (packet FIFO)?? Packet mode requires TLAST and drops/preserves packets — overkill. 

  Alternative bulletproof: skip axis_data_fifo IP entirely — use **FIFO Generator** (fifo_generator v13.2) first-word-fall-through sync FIFO 80-bit wide × 512: classic interface (wr_en/rd_en/full/empty), which I handshake to AXIS myself in 10 lines (tvalid=rdy&~empty... need FWFT: dout valid when ~empty). FIFO Generator is rock-solid headless: create_ip fifo_generator with CONFIG.Fifo_Implementation=Common_Clock_Block_RAM, Input_Data_Width=80, Input_Depth=512, Performance_Options=First_Word_Fall_Through.

  My own AXIS shim on top (5 lines):
  ```
  // write side (B RX): wr = b_rx_tvalid & ~full
  // read side (B TX): m_tvalid = ~empty; b_tx_tvalid = ~empty & m_tready?? 
  ```
  Careful AXIS→FWFT handshake: consumer tready. Aurora TX: tvalid must not toggle arbitrarily? AXIS allows tvalid independent of tready: drive tvalid=~empty, tdata=dout, consume (rd_en) when tvalid&tready. With FWFT: rd_en pops next word; dout updates. Correct pattern:
  ```
  assign b_tx_tvalid = ~fifo_empty;
  assign b_tx_tdata  = fifo_dout;
  assign fifo_rd_en  = b_tx_tvalid & b_tx_tready;   // pop when accepted
  ```
